[h1]RimCBM[/h1]
[i]RimWorld 1.6 · Alpha · Requires Harmony[/i]

Plan your implants around [b]body space, power and maintenance[/b]. Inspired by the CBM concept in Cataclysm: Dark Days Ahead, RimCBM brings shaped implant modules and body grids to RimWorld.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*]Fit modules into body-region grids. Bionic parts and expansion implants provide additional room.
[*]Surgery prepares an implant; your pawn completes deployment and rearrangement actions. Research unlocks same-board rearrangement.
[*]Hot swapping works only when both the implant and every occupied cell support it.
[*]Manage shared W / Wd storage, generators, fuel, charging stations and automatic supply policies.
[*]Use passive, toggle, one-shot and reactive abilities through a native Gizmo and target context menus.
[*]Maintain damaged, contaminated or unsterile implants. Fire, EMP, burden and configurable faults create trade-offs.
[*]An expandable Health panel manages your layout. Research lives in a separate Implants tab.
[/list]

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
Enable Harmony before RimCBM. Open a pawn's Health tab and press CBM. Use + to schedule surgery, then drag a prepared module into valid cells. Right-click implants for removal options; use the Gizmo for abilities and supply settings.

[h2]Alpha status[/h2]
This is a working framework with prototype modules, not CDDA's complete implant catalogue. Content, research progression, artwork and balance are still being developed. Developer fixtures are excluded from normal trader stock. Core features do not require DLC. Combat Extended and third-party race/electricity integrations are not certified.

